We have $\sin A = \frac{BC}{AC}$ and $\cos A = \frac{AB}{AC}$, so $2\sin A = 3\cos B$ gives us $2\cdot \frac{BC}{AC} = 3\cdot\frac{AB}{AC}$.  Multiplying both sides by $AC$ gives $2BC = 3AB$, so $\frac{BC}{AB} = \frac{3}{2}$.  Finally, we have $\tan A = \frac{BC}{AB} = \boxed{\frac{3}{2}}$.

We also could have noted that $2\sin A = 3\cos A$ gives us $\sin A = \frac32\cos A$, so $\tan A = \frac{\sin A}{\cos A} = \frac{(3/2)\cos A}{\cos A } =\boxed{\frac32}$.

